WEBVTT

NOTE Tube Scan Plan Guide — Normal Beam TCG Calibration
NOTE Language: English (en)
NOTE Source: Adam v6 narration via ElevenLabs eleven_v3

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.620
TCG calibration for
normal beam inspection.

2
00:00:03.520 --> 00:00:05.660
In this video, you will
learn how to create,

3
00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:09.320
verify, and save a TCG
setup in ScanMaster.

4
00:00:10.520 --> 00:00:12.940
Before you start, prepare six items,

5
00:00:13.680 --> 00:00:16.200
the ScanMaster System,
a normal beam probe,

6
00:00:16.880 --> 00:00:20.020
a calibration block with at
least three FBH reflectors,

7
00:00:20.440 --> 00:00:22.400
the correct material
velocity for the material,

8
00:00:23.020 --> 00:00:26.340
a stable water path, and
access to Teach In mode.

9
00:00:27.180 --> 00:00:29.760
Once everything is ready,
open the ScanMaster Wizard.

10
00:00:30.920 --> 00:00:34.140
On the calibration block,
three FBH standards at

11
00:00:34.140 --> 00:00:36.420
different depths will
work from near to far,

12
00:00:37.180 --> 00:00:41.920
standard one, near, standard
two, middle, standard three, far.

13
00:00:42.840 --> 00:00:44.240
Open the ScanMaster Wizard.

14
00:00:44.920 --> 00:00:46.820
From the main menu, click Teach In.

15
00:00:47.360 --> 00:00:48.380
A new screen image appears,

16
00:00:49.020 --> 00:00:51.520
the instrument window plus
the Setup Toolbox dialog.

17
00:00:52.580 --> 00:00:54.380
First, set the basic parameters.

18
00:00:55.080 --> 00:00:57.740
Four fields. One. Material velocity.

19
00:00:58.820 --> 00:01:00.000
From the material database,

20
00:01:00.260 --> 00:01:03.500
select the material you're
inspecting. Two. Range.

21
00:01:04.280 --> 00:01:07.720
Set the range until you see the
back wall. Three. Gain.

22
00:01:08.420 --> 00:01:13.860
Verify the response from the
3/64-inch FBH. Four. Water path.

23
00:01:14.300 --> 00:01:17.980
Set 76 millimeters, or set the
transducer to surface distance,

24
00:01:18.340 --> 00:01:20.400
so the second front
reflection does not appear

25
00:01:20.400 --> 00:01:23.100
between the first front
and first back reflections.

26
00:01:23.920 --> 00:01:24.620
Important.

27
00:01:25.140 --> 00:01:27.720
Keep the water path
consistent within plus or

28
00:01:27.720 --> 00:01:30.460
minus one quarter inch
during standardization,

29
00:01:30.720 --> 00:01:32.860
initial scanning, and final evaluation.

30
00:01:33.700 --> 00:01:35.320
Deviation beyond plus or

31
00:01:35.320 --> 00:01:38.160
minus a quarter inch
requires re-standardization.

32
00:01:38.980 --> 00:01:42.880
Before we set anything else,
understand what TCG is solving.

33
00:01:43.600 --> 00:01:46.920
Before TCG, three identical
flat bottom holes,

34
00:01:47.400 --> 00:01:48.580
three different signal heights.

35
00:01:49.180 --> 00:01:51.680
Closer means stronger,
farther means weaker.

36
00:01:52.360 --> 00:01:57.340
After TCG, all FBH responses
adjusted to 80% FSH.

37
00:01:57.960 --> 00:02:00.640
One reference level.
One pass-fail criterion.

38
00:02:01.420 --> 00:02:02.100
Across depth.

39
00:02:02.800 --> 00:02:03.820
That is our goal.

40
00:02:04.440 --> 00:02:05.060
Let's build it.

41
00:02:05.820 --> 00:02:09.080
Inside the Setup Toolbox,
click the TCG tab.

42
00:02:09.720 --> 00:02:11.020
The TCG table appears.

43
00:02:11.780 --> 00:02:14.300
Before any other action,
verify three checkboxes

44
00:02:14.300 --> 00:02:16.500
on the right side of the TCG tab.

45
00:02:16.960 --> 00:02:18.860
Active, Visible, Drag.

46
00:02:19.680 --> 00:02:20.980
All three must be checked.

47
00:02:21.360 --> 00:02:23.440
If Drag is off, you cannot drag

48
00:02:23.440 --> 00:02:25.020
the yellow dots in the next steps.

49
00:02:25.820 --> 00:02:27.560
The same action, repeated three times.

50
00:02:28.040 --> 00:02:29.080
Set point one,

51
00:02:29.860 --> 00:02:32.100
near FBH at 80% FSH.

52
00:02:32.700 --> 00:02:36.420
Set point two, middle FBH at 80% FSH.

53
00:02:37.080 --> 00:02:40.920
Set point three, far FBH at 80% FSH.

54
00:02:41.520 --> 00:02:44.240
Drag yellow dot. 80% FSH.

55
00:02:44.880 --> 00:02:46.220
Save. Three times.

56
00:02:47.080 --> 00:02:50.000
Move the probe to the first
FBH, the near standard.

57
00:02:50.980 --> 00:02:54.460
On the A-scan, drag the yellow
dot onto the response peak.

58
00:02:55.280 --> 00:02:59.700
Adjust the Gain so the FBH
amplitude reaches 80% FSH.

59
00:03:00.800 --> 00:03:02.740
As you turn Gain up, the trace rises.

60
00:03:03.400 --> 00:03:05.900
Stop when the peak touches
the cyan reference line.

61
00:03:06.940 --> 00:03:07.680
Save Point one.

62
00:03:08.500 --> 00:03:10.480
Click the Save button
on the toolbar setup.

63
00:03:11.360 --> 00:03:12.540
Node one — locked.

64
00:03:13.960 --> 00:03:16.640
Move the probe to the second
FBH, the middle standard.

65
00:03:17.340 --> 00:03:20.300
Drag the second yellow dot
onto the new response peak.

66
00:03:21.040 --> 00:03:25.140
Adjust Gain so this peak
also reaches 80% FSH.

67
00:03:25.820 --> 00:03:28.800
Save Point two. Node two — locked.

68
00:03:29.600 --> 00:03:32.860
Move the probe to the third
FBH, the far standard.

69
00:03:33.700 --> 00:03:36.300
Drag the third yellow dot
onto the response peak.

70
00:03:37.040 --> 00:03:39.440
Adjust Gain to 80% FSH.

71
00:03:40.280 --> 00:03:43.340
Save Point three. Node three — locked.

72
00:03:44.520 --> 00:03:45.960
Three reference points set.

73
00:03:46.460 --> 00:03:47.900
One detail from the guide.

74
00:03:48.640 --> 00:03:49.820
With more than three segments,

75
00:03:50.280 --> 00:03:52.800
scroll boxes appear to the
right of the segment list.

76
00:03:53.480 --> 00:03:56.440
The active segment is marked
with an arrow next to its number.

77
00:03:57.340 --> 00:03:59.680
If your inspection extends
to full part depth,

78
00:04:00.080 --> 00:04:02.420
add a TCG point on the back-wall response.

79
00:04:03.400 --> 00:04:05.020
Click the toolbar button to set the

80
00:04:05.020 --> 00:04:07.120
first point before the back-wall pulse.

81
00:04:08.060 --> 00:04:10.200
Then the second point
after the back-wall pulse.

82
00:04:10.960 --> 00:04:14.040
Create at least four points in total to

83
00:04:14.040 --> 00:04:16.800
define the TCG curve through
the back-wall response.

84
00:04:17.660 --> 00:04:18.140
Optional.

85
00:04:18.800 --> 00:04:20.100
Skip this step if your inspection

86
00:04:20.100 --> 00:04:22.320
only covers the FBH depth range.

87
00:04:23.180 --> 00:04:25.020
Now save the TCG setup.

88
00:04:25.580 --> 00:04:26.140
Four clicks.

89
00:04:27.220 --> 00:04:30.180
One. Click the Files tab
in the Setup Toolbox.

90
00:04:30.920 --> 00:04:33.480
Two. Under TCG, click Save.

91
00:04:34.440 --> 00:04:37.860
Three. The UPRDB Navigator dialog opens.

92
00:04:38.500 --> 00:04:40.620
The default file path is
displayed at the bottom.

93
00:04:41.220 --> 00:04:42.900
Four. Name the file.

94
00:04:43.580 --> 00:04:46.560
We recommend a naming convention
that includes the probe type,

95
00:04:47.000 --> 00:04:48.940
the FBH size and the date.

96
00:04:49.600 --> 00:04:52.880
For example, Normal Beam
underscore TCG underscore

97
00:04:53.720 --> 00:04:56.440
3/64-inch FBH underscore today's date.

98
00:04:57.240 --> 00:04:57.700
Click Save.

99
00:04:58.420 --> 00:04:59.780
TCG setup saved.

100
00:05:00.940 --> 00:05:02.920
Quick checklist before
you run the inspection.

101
00:05:03.820 --> 00:05:08.020
Teach In opened. Material
velocity set. Range set.

102
00:05:08.500 --> 00:05:11.500
Water path kept within plus
or minus a quarter inch.

103
00:05:12.060 --> 00:05:15.420
Three FBH responses set to 80% FSH.

104
00:05:16.180 --> 00:05:18.660
Optional back-wall points added if needed.

105
00:05:19.340 --> 00:05:20.520
TCG setup saved.

106
00:05:21.360 --> 00:05:22.620
Your TCG is ready.

107
00:05:23.260 --> 00:05:23.740
Run the inspection.

108
00:05:24.960 --> 00:05:27.340
If you need to recalibrate
after a probe change,

109
00:05:27.900 --> 00:05:30.740
a material change or any
deviation in water path,

110
00:05:31.100 --> 00:05:32.260
return to step three.

111
00:05:32.980 --> 00:05:35.460
The full Scan Plan documentation is

112
00:05:35.460 --> 00:05:37.120
available in the Scan Plan tab.
